{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966970,"nonce":"DUROo7bSg1bhouwXYr5nRqCqWao=","title":"DSL collections stop at Vec\u003cT\u003e for scalar T; a list of structs needs a layout","message":"A `.blinc` list literal lowers to `List\u003cT\u003e { data, len, capacity }`, so a\nprop crosses as one pointer and nothing marshals per element. The stride\nfollows the declared element type, which is why the decoder is selected\nfrom `Vec\u003cT\u003e` rather than assumed.\n\nThat only works while `T` is a scalar. A list of structs needs the\nelement layout to cross too, and it does not today.\n\nThis is the blocker under both `cn.Table` and `cn.Chart`: a row is not a\nscalar, so neither widget can take its data until this lands.","files":null}]}